Yes, to contract lycanthropy from a monster bite, the monster does need 
to hit you. All currently existing lycanthropes in vanilla (and 
SLASH'EM, for that matter) spread the condition through biting in 
animal form, so the attack must also get past your MC. This makes MC3 
and/or sufficiently negative AC effective, but imperfect defenses (e.g. 
still a 1/50 chance to get past MC3).

A ring of protection from shape changers also provides an indirect 
defense against lycanthropy (forces them into human form, so they can't 
infect you via attacks), and an amulet of unchanging will stop you from 
going into animal form (you can still be infected, but won't change at 
inopportune times). Polymorph control will also let you choose to 
decline a change in form, according to its wiki article.

